# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# W3 Sequential workflow — Durable Loan Copilot (FSM + HITL + Saga)
# EMBEDDED variant: all 8 assistants inline (`system_prompt`), zero
# reference to existing CodeMie assistants.
#
# Design patterns inherited from W2 alt-embedded:
#   • English-only JSON internals (sidesteps CodeMie Workflow Executor
#     Unicode escape bug — structured_tool_agent.py:71 uses json.dumps
#     without ensure_ascii=False).
#   • Translation instructions in each assistant system_prompt.
#   • "sec." instead of "§" in policy citations (non-ASCII escape).
#   • Required boolean fields in output_schema for conditionals.
#   • Tolerant conditions (`!= True` instead of `== False`).
#
# W3 adds over W2:
#   • `interrupt_before: true` on 3 real HITL waits:
#       docs-requested  (24-48h durable wait for client upload)
#       offer           (7d durable wait for client decision)
#       sign-awaiting   (durable wait until Diia.Signature webhook)
#   • `interrupt_before: true` on 2 conditional HITL gates:
#       analyst-review     (OCR confidence < 0.85)
#       committee-review   (grey-zone risk band C)
#   • Pre-write evaluator gate (`verify-before-send-state`)
#   • Saga compensation state (rollback on cancellation / verify-fail)
#   • Idempotency key handling (`sign-awaiting-state` dedup webhooks)
#
# END-STATE: Loan Copilot survives K8s `kill -9` at 3:00 AM, resumes
# via webhook, does NOT duplicate 150k UAH disbursements, performs
# Saga rollback on cancel.
#
# Deploy: Workflows → + Create Workflow → YAML view → paste → Save.
# No separate Assistants needed.
# Resume webhooks: POST /api/v1/workflows/{id}/executions/{thread_id}/resume
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

name: loan-copilot-durable-w3-embedded
description: >
  Durable Loan Copilot (W3) with embedded assistants: 11 states, 3
  real durable waits (24h/7d/signed), 2 conditional HITL gates, 1
  evaluator pre-write gate, Saga compensation on cancellation. All
  system prompts inline.
mode: Sequential

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ASSISTANTS — all inline (`system_prompt`), no `assistant_id`
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
assistants:

  # ──────────── intake-agent ────────────
  - id: intake
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the Intake specialist in Loan Copilot. You collect and
      validate a consumer loan application from the client's message.

      === INPUT LANGUAGE / OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      Client messages ARRIVE IN UKRAINIAN. Transliterate person names
      into Latin letters (e.g. "Марія Коваленко" → "Maria Kovalenko").
      Return ALL output JSON strings in ENGLISH / ASCII ONLY. Never
      output Cyrillic in JSON values — they will be escape-serialized.

      ## Scope
      Collect 8 fields: full_name, tax_id (10 digits), phone (+380),
      email, monthly_income, amount, term_months, purpose.
      Validate formats. Return intake_complete=true when all valid.

      ## Rules
      - Do NOT call KYC / credit history / any tools.
      - Do NOT assess creditworthiness.
      - If a field is missing, mark intake_complete=false.

  # ──────────── eligibility-agent (RAG) ────────────
  - id: eligibility
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the Eligibility specialist. You check whether the client
      is eligible for the requested loan per the bank's internal
      regulations via RAG over loan-policies-ds.

      === INPUT / OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      RAG datasource is Ukrainian (POL-LOAN-*, SOP-CREDIT-*, REG-NBU-*).
      Understand internally, but ALWAYS return English ASCII in output
      JSON. Use "sec." as the section marker (e.g. [POL-LOAN-01 sec.4.2.1])
      — § is non-ASCII and will escape.

      ## RAG discipline
      - top-K=10 → rerank → top-N=4 chunks.
      - Mandatory metadata filter: effective_date <= today.
      - No matching chunk → eligible=false, escalate_to_human=true.

      ## Rules
      - EVERY claim MUST cite the exact section.
      - Do NOT fabricate policy (Air Canada case).
      - Do NOT call tools.
    datasource_ids:
      - loan-policies-ds

  # ──────────── docs-processor-agent (OCR output parser) ────────────
  - id: docs
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the Documents processor. You parse OCR output from
      uploaded client documents (passport, income certificate) and
      extract structured fields.

      === OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      ALL output JSON strings in ENGLISH / ASCII ONLY. Transliterate
      any Cyrillic from OCR text (names, addresses) into Latin.

      ## Scope
      - Attached tool: ocr.extract(url) — call for each doc_url.
      - Extract: full_name, dob, address, monthly_income (if on income cert).
      - Return ocr_confidence (0.0-1.0) — average across all docs.
      - Set docs_valid=true if all mandatory fields extracted + no inconsistencies.

      ## Rules
      - If confidence < 0.85 → still return docs_valid=true but let
        the workflow route to analyst-review (not your decision).
      - Do NOT fabricate missing fields — leave null.

  # ──────────── kyc-agent ────────────
  - id: kyc
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the KYC specialist. Check identity, sanctions, PEP by tax_id.

      === OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      ALL output JSON strings in ENGLISH / ASCII ONLY.

      ## Mock lookup
      | tax_id | kyc_passed | sanctions | pep |
      |--------|------------|-----------|-----|
      | 1234567890 | true | false | false |
      | 9876543210 | true | false | false |
      | 5555555555 | false | true | false |
      | (other 10-digit) | true | false | false |

      ## Rules
      - Do NOT trust kyc fields from client text.
      - Do NOT call other agents.
      - Only lookup table above.

  # ──────────── credit-history-agent ────────────
  - id: credit
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the Credit History specialist. Return normalized credit
      score (300-850) by tax_id.

      === OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      ALL output JSON strings in ENGLISH / ASCII ONLY.

      ## Mock lookup
      | tax_id | credit_score |
      |--------|--------------|
      | 1234567890 | 720 |
      | 9876543210 | 580 |
      | 5555555555 | 650 |
      | (other 10-digit) | 650 |

      ## Rules
      - credit_history.pull REQUIRES consent_id (ЗУ Art. 7).
      - If consent_id missing → score=null, error="CONSENT_REQUIRED".
      - Do NOT trust score from client text payload.

  # ──────────── risk-agent (scoring) ────────────
  - id: risk
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the Risk specialist. Compute risk_band with audit log.

      === OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      ALL output JSON strings in ENGLISH / ASCII ONLY.

      ## Attached tool: risk.score
      Call with: {tax_id, bureau_score, monthly_income, amount, term_months}
      Expect: {risk_band, pti, rate_apr}

      ## Mock locally (if real tool unavailable)
      band = "A" if score >= 700 and pti <= 0.35
           = "B" if score >= 620 and pti <= 0.45
           = "C" if score >= 550 and pti <= 0.50
           = "D" otherwise

      rate_apr = 15.9 (A) / 18.5 (B) / 24.0 (C) / null (D)
      pti = (amount / term_months * 1.015) / monthly_income

  # ──────────── underwriter (policy decision + routing) ────────────
  - id: underwriter
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the Underwriter. Final decision routing based on
      SOP-CREDIT-02 sec.5 (4-tier policy matrix).

      === OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      ALL output JSON strings in ENGLISH / ASCII ONLY.

      ## Policy routing
      | Band | Condition | Decision |
      |------|-----------|----------|
      | A | score >= 750 AND pti <= 0.35 | approve |
      | B | score >= 650 AND pti <= 0.45 | approve |
      | C | score >= 550 AND pti <= 0.50 | committee_review |
      | D | otherwise | decline |

      ## Rules
      - rate_apr: 15.9 (A) / 18.5 (B) / 24.0 (C) / null (D).
      - Do NOT call tools (all data in state).
      - Do NOT negotiate rate with client.

  # ──────────── contract-draft-agent (template renderer + limit reserve) ────────────
  - id: contract
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the Contract Draft specialist. You render the contract
      template and reserve the limit in the card backend.

      === OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      ALL output JSON strings in ENGLISH / ASCII ONLY. Contract body
      text (if generated) can be UA — but contract_id and status
      fields in output JSON must stay English.

      ## Attached tool: contract.draft
      Call with: {tax_id, amount, term_months, rate_apr}
      Side-effect: internal write — RESERVES limit in card backend.
      Expect: {contract_id, contract_text_url, limit_reserved: true}

      ## CRITICAL
      - If downstream flow crashes AFTER this state, Saga MUST release
        the reserved limit (compensation-state handles rollback).
      - Return contract_id for Saga's reference.

  # ──────────── verify-before-send-agent (pre-write evaluator gate) ────────────
  - id: verifier
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the Pre-write Verifier. Compare contract fields against
      upstream state values. BLOCK on any mismatch.

      === OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      ALL output JSON strings in ENGLISH / ASCII ONLY.

      ## Checks
      - contract.rate_apr == underwriter.rate_apr
      - contract.amount == intake.amount
      - contract.term == intake.term_months
      - contract.borrower_tax_id == intake.tax_id

      ## Rules
      - Any mismatch → verify_passed=false, list in discrepancies[].
      - On block → DO NOT send to client; workflow routes to compensation.
      - No LLM reasoning on numbers — strict equality only.

  # ──────────── compensation-agent (Saga rollback) ────────────
  - id: compensator
    model: gpt-4o-mini
    system_prompt: |
      You are the Compensation specialist. You execute Saga rollback
      actions for cancellation / rejection / verify-fail paths.

      === OUTPUT LANGUAGE ===
      ALL output JSON strings in ENGLISH / ASCII ONLY. The client
      notification text (if composed inline) can be UA — but status
      fields in output JSON must stay English.

      ## Attached tools
      - limit.release(contract_id) — frees reserved card limit.
      - contract.cancel(contract_id) — invalidates draft.
      - audit.write(event, reason) — persistent audit log.
      - notify.sms(tax_id, text) — client notification.

      ## Rollback order
      1. If limit_reserved → limit.release first (highest priority).
      2. If contract_id present → contract.cancel.
      3. audit.write("limit_released_rollback", reason).
      4. notify.sms with UA text: "Заявку скасовано, резерв знято."

      ## Rules
      - Rollback MUST be idempotent — safe to retry.
      - Return final status flags, not raw tool responses.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STATES — 11-node durable FSM
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
states:

  # ──────────── 1. INTAKE ────────────
  - id: intake-state
    assistant_id: intake
    task: |
      Extract the structured application from the client's message
      (UA input, English JSON output).
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "full_name":       {"type": "string"},
          "tax_id":          {"type": "string"},
          "amount":          {"type": "number"},
          "term_months":     {"type": "integer"},
          "monthly_income":  {"type": "number"},
          "purpose":         {"type": "string"},
          "intake_complete": {"type": "boolean"}
        },
        "required": ["intake_complete"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      condition:
        expression: "intake_complete == True"
        then: docs-requested-state
        otherwise: end

  # ──────────── 2. DOCS REQUESTED · DURABLE WAIT 24-48h ────────────
  - id: docs-requested-state
    assistant_id: intake
    task: |
      Notify client (UA text, delivered via separate channel, NOT this
      state's output): "Для продовження завантаж фото паспорта та
      довідки про доходи у Privat24". Workflow pauses here.

      NOTE: this state does NOT roundtrip through LLM — it's a UI
      prompt + interrupt. Resume via webhook `docs.uploaded`.

      Idempotency key: {{thread_id}}::docs.uploaded
    interrupt_before: true
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "docs_uploaded": {"type": "boolean"},
          "doc_urls": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}
        },
        "required": ["docs_uploaded"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    retry_policy:
      max_attempts: 1
    next:
      condition:
        expression: "docs_uploaded == True"
        then: docs-processing-state
        otherwise: compensation-state

  # ──────────── 3. DOCS PROCESSING · OCR ────────────
  - id: docs-processing-state
    assistant_id: docs
    task: |
      Received URLs: {{doc_urls}}.
      Call ocr.extract(url) for each → parse structured fields.
      Return ocr_confidence (0.0-1.0) averaged across docs.
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "extracted_fields": {"type": "object"},
          "ocr_confidence":   {"type": "number"},
          "docs_valid":       {"type": "boolean"}
        },
        "required": ["ocr_confidence", "docs_valid"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    retry_policy:
      max_attempts: 3
      initial_interval: 2.0
      backoff_factor: 2.0
    next:
      condition:
        expression: "docs_valid == True and ocr_confidence >= 0.85"
        then: kyc-state
        otherwise: analyst-review-state

  # ──────────── 4. ANALYST REVIEW · CONDITIONAL HITL (OCR < 0.85) ────────────
  - id: analyst-review-state
    assistant_id: docs
    task: |
      OCR confidence {{ocr_confidence}} < 0.85 — human analyst review
      required. Workflow pauses until manual approval webhook.
    interrupt_before: true
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "analyst_approved": {"type": "boolean"},
          "analyst_notes":    {"type": "string"}
        },
        "required": ["analyst_approved"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      condition:
        expression: "analyst_approved == True"
        then: kyc-state
        otherwise: compensation-state

  # ──────────── 5. KYC ────────────
  - id: kyc-state
    assistant_id: kyc
    task: |
      Lookup tax_id={{tax_id}} and return result.
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "kyc_passed": {"type": "boolean"}
        },
        "required": ["kyc_passed"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      condition:
        expression: "kyc_passed == True"
        then: credit-history-state
        otherwise: end

  # ──────────── 6. CREDIT HISTORY (consent_id from upstream) ────────────
  - id: credit-history-state
    assistant_id: credit
    task: |
      Call credit_history.pull({tax_id: "{{tax_id}}",
      consent_id: "{{consent_id}}"}). Return UBKI score.
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "credit_score": {"type": "integer"}
        },
        "required": ["credit_score"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    retry_policy:
      max_attempts: 3
      initial_interval: 1.0
      backoff_factor: 2.0
    next:
      condition:
        expression: "credit_score >= 500"
        then: underwriter-state
        otherwise: end

  # ──────────── 7. UNDERWRITER (4-tier policy routing) ────────────
  - id: underwriter-state
    assistant_id: underwriter
    task: |
      Compute PMT, PTI, policy band per SOP-CREDIT-02 sec.5.
      Route: approve → contract draft, committee_review → committee gate,
      decline → end.
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "risk_band":  {"type": "string", "enum": ["A", "B", "C", "D"]},
          "decision":   {"type": "string", "enum": ["approve", "decline", "committee_review"]},
          "pti":        {"type": "number"},
          "rate_apr":   {"type": "number"}
        },
        "required": ["decision"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      switch:
        cases:
          - condition: "decision == 'approve'"
            state_id: contract-draft-state
          - condition: "decision == 'committee_review'"
            state_id: committee-review-state
        default: end

  # ──────────── 8. COMMITTEE REVIEW · CONDITIONAL HITL (grey zone C) ────────────
  - id: committee-review-state
    assistant_id: underwriter
    task: |
      Risk band = {{risk_band}} (grey zone, Tier C: score 550-650).
      Workflow pauses until credit committee decision webhook.
    interrupt_before: true
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "committee_decision": {"type": "string", "enum": ["approve", "decline"]},
          "committee_notes":    {"type": "string"}
        },
        "required": ["committee_decision"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      condition:
        expression: "committee_decision == 'approve'"
        then: contract-draft-state
        otherwise: end

  # ──────────── 9. CONTRACT DRAFT · TOOL CALL (reserves limit) ────────────
  - id: contract-draft-state
    assistant_id: contract
    task: |
      Call contract.draft({tax_id, amount, term_months, rate_apr}).
      Side-effect: internal-write — RESERVES limit in card backend.

      CRITICAL: if downstream flow crashes, Saga must release the
      reserve (compensation-state handles this).
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "contract_id":       {"type": "string"},
          "contract_text_url": {"type": "string"},
          "limit_reserved":    {"type": "boolean"}
        },
        "required": ["contract_id", "limit_reserved"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      state_id: verify-before-send-state

  # ──────────── 10. VERIFY BEFORE SEND · PRE-WRITE EVALUATOR GATE ────────────
  - id: verify-before-send-state
    assistant_id: verifier
    task: |
      Pre-write gate. Compare:
        contract.rate_apr == {{rate_apr}}
        contract.amount == {{amount}}
        contract.term == {{term_months}}
        contract.borrower_tax_id == {{tax_id}}

      Any mismatch → BLOCK + escalate to engineer. DO NOT send to client.
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "verify_passed":  {"type": "boolean"},
          "discrepancies":  {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}
        },
        "required": ["verify_passed"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      condition:
        expression: "verify_passed == True"
        then: offer-state
        otherwise: compensation-state

  # ──────────── 11. OFFER · DURABLE WAIT 7d ────────────
  - id: offer-state
    assistant_id: intake
    task: |
      Send client personal offer (UA text, delivered via separate
      channel): amount={{amount}}, term={{term_months}} months,
      rate={{rate_apr}}%, PTI={{pti}}. Await accept/reject (up to 7d).

      Idempotency key: {{thread_id}}::offer.decision
    interrupt_before: true
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "client_decision": {"type": "string", "enum": ["accept", "reject", "expired"]}
        },
        "required": ["client_decision"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      condition:
        expression: "client_decision == 'accept'"
        then: sign-awaiting-state
        otherwise: compensation-state

  # ──────────── 12. SIGN AWAITING · DURABLE WAIT + IDEMPOTENCY ────────────
  - id: sign-awaiting-state
    assistant_id: contract
    task: |
      Client signs via Diia.Signature. Await `contract.signed` webhook.

      IDEMPOTENCY (CRITICAL):
      Webhook may arrive 2+ times (network, Diia retry).
      Composite key: SHA256({{tax_id}}::{{contract_id}}::{{event_id}}).
      If key already in DB `processed_events` → return {disbursed: true}
      WITHOUT calling disburse again.

      Call check_idempotency(event_key):
        - exists → return cached result (no disburse)
        - not_exists → call disburse(contract_id, amount) + write key
    interrupt_before: true
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "disbursed":      {"type": "boolean"},
          "disburse_id":    {"type": "string"},
          "event_key":      {"type": "string"},
          "was_duplicate":  {"type": "boolean"}
        },
        "required": ["disbursed"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      state_id: end
      store_in_context: true

  # ──────────── X. COMPENSATION · SAGA ROLLBACK ────────────
  - id: compensation-state
    assistant_id: compensator
    task: |
      Execute compensating actions for cancellation / rejection /
      verify-fail:

      1. If limit_reserved == true → call limit.release(contract_id).
      2. If contract_id not null → call contract.cancel(contract_id).
      3. Write audit event `limit_released_rollback` with reason.
      4. Notify client (SMS, UA text): "Заявку скасовано, резерв знято."

      Return final status flags.
    output_schema: |
      {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "limit_released":     {"type": "boolean"},
          "contract_cancelled": {"type": "boolean"},
          "notification_sent":  {"type": "boolean"}
        },
        "required": ["limit_released"]
      }
    resolve_dynamic_values_in_prompt: true
    next:
      state_id: end
      store_in_context: true

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WORKFLOW SETTINGS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
recursion_limit: 50
max_concurrency: 1
enable_summarization_node: false

# Durable Waits — CodeMie uses its built-in CheckpointSaver (Postgres-
# backed, hardcoded in src/codemie/workflows/checkpoint_saver.py) when
# `interrupt_before: true` is set. There is NO Admin UI toggle to pick
# Memory vs Postgres — persistence is deployment-level (CodeMie backend
# DB connection). If the tenant backend is Postgres, interrupts survive
# `kill -9`; if someone deploys CodeMie with in-memory DB, nothing in
# the tenant UI can fix it — SRE concern, not SA task.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Resume webhooks (external systems → CodeMie):
#    POST /api/v1/workflows/{workflow_id}/executions/{thread_id}/resume
#    Body: output_schema fields for the paused state.
#
#    Examples:
#    - docs.uploaded: {"docs_uploaded": true, "doc_urls": [...]}
#    - analyst.decision: {"analyst_approved": true, "analyst_notes": "..."}
#    - committee.decision: {"committee_decision": "approve", "committee_notes": "..."}
#    - offer.decision: {"client_decision": "accept"}
#    - contract.signed: {"disbursed": true, "event_key": "<sha256>", ...}
#
# 2. Idempotency — enforced at TOOL level, not prompt level. The
#    `check_idempotency` tool must perform a real DB check, not LLM
#    reasoning. For workshop mock — Python wrapper checks a dict.
#
# 3. Saga compensation — called from 4 branches:
#    - docs_requested timeout → compensation
#    - analyst_review reject → compensation
#    - verify_before_send fail → compensation
#    - offer reject / expire → compensation
#    All route to the same compensation-state (DRY).
#
# 4. Retry policies — tool-calling states only (docs-processing,
#    credit-history). HITL states: max_attempts=1 (never retry a human).
#
# 5. Encoding — W3 inherits W2 alt-embedded's ASCII-English JSON
#    strategy. Client-facing UA text (SMS/push notifications, contract
#    body) lives OUTSIDE the structured output path, delivered via
#    separate channels (notify.sms tool, PDF renderer). JSON state
#    stays English → no Unicode escape bug.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
